for many children logging on to the  internet is the first thing they do in  the morning  88 percent of german children go online  every  day a smartphone is a game console tv  music player and communications device  all-in-one  in my class we all use a class chat app  and if i wasn't on it i'd miss out on  everything like if i forgot my homework  i can't really imagine what i'd do  without my smartphone  in most families children are more  computer savvy than their parents  hard-working moms and dads can hardly  keep up with the newest trends  it requires so much energy to always  have to check to see what they're doing  to have that feeling i need to know what  they're up to  it's especially hard to supervise older  children for teenagers with a smartphone  sex and violence are always just a few  clicks away  many young adults post their own videos  online before thinking about the  long-term consequences  it can start out innocently enough a  young person sends a selfie to a friend  but a photo sometimes falls into the  wrong hands  one in three teenagers has experienced  cyber bullying  i know someone who took a photo of  herself in a bikini then on a class trip  someone stole her smartphone and sent  the photo to all of her contacts  personal photos unintentionally posted  for all the world to see cyber bullies  use the internet to publicly humiliate  their victims  there was a boy in my school and he got  bullied because he smelled bad  there are a lot of photos of him posted  online with the word stinker written  underneath  experts take cyber mobbing seriously but  it can be difficult to protect a child  from vicious cyber attacks  you should deal with the issue right  away  tell the teacher if necessary if it gets  really bad if it's posted on facebook or  twitter  then you should have the post removed  and maybe call the police  another problematic issue violent video  games  many parents don't want their kids  exposed to them but age restrictions are  hard to enforce most kids find ways to  download their favorite games  youth protection programs can help  parents safeguard their children  they can download programs like the  kidsafe browser or k9 the applications  work on most tablets and smartphones  they filter out internet content not  deemed age appropriate  the software automatically installs a  list of prohibited and approved websites  the programs also warn users against  unsolicited subscriptions and illegal  downloads parents should also turn off  so-called download helper programs  but so far there is still no way to make  the internet completely kid safe experts  say a costly mistake could teach a child  an important life  in lesson one has to understand that if  you're unlucky one wrong mouse click can  cost mom or dad or yourself a lot of  money getting misled on the internet can  be a good learning experience  children with smartphones also run the  risk of spending too much time online  german children spend around three hours  a day surfing the web  on weekends it's sometimes even longer  german researchers developed the app  mental to help users keep track of their  internet use  the app tells me i accessed my  smartphone 97 times yesterday i sent  zero text messages made zero phone calls  but i spent over six hours online  that's crazy  shift says time to put down your  smartphone
 

